project: savantenvs/fcc
target: fcc-buggy-mhh-run-14

# File-input (CLI) target: feed the fuzz bytes as a C source file to fcc, the small self-hosting C
# compiler. `-S` runs the WHOLE front end (lexer, preprocessor/`using`, parser, analyzer, type checker)
# and the x86 code emitter, writing assembly and STOPPING before it would shell out to `cc` to
# assemble/link — so the fuzz surface is the compiler itself, with no assembler/linker dependency.
# Not libFuzzer: the natural fuzz surface is the compiler on a source file.
#
# `filepath:` + a literal path (not `@@`) is the ORIGINAL harness's form — mayhemheroes/fcc's
# Mayhemfile at a9511b3854 ran /fcc/bin/release/fcc on a literal /test.c with `filepath: /test.c` — and
# it is what this target needs: fcc writes its `.s` intermediate NEXT TO THE INPUT (src/options.c:150,
# `filext(input, "s")`, which `-o` does not override) and src/asm.c:asmInit() never NULL-checks that
# fopen(), so the input must sit in a writable directory. `filepath:` guarantees exactly that — Mayhem
# writes the testcase there itself — whereas `@@` resolves into Mayhem's read-only testcase mount, where
# EVERY input, valid C included, dies in the first asmOutLn(). The only departures from the original are
# the path (`/tmp/…`, since this image runs as uid 2000 and cannot write `/`) and `-S`, which drops the
# assemble/link step so no 32-bit `cc`/`as`/`ld` toolchain is needed at fuzz time.
#
# The bugs this replays are fcc's own faults — a NULL member access in the error/type printers
# (src/type.c:546, src/error.c) and an integer division by zero in the constant evaluator
# (src/eval.c:104-105) — surfacing as SIGSEGV / SIGFPE with the recursion that reached them, the way the
# original gcc-built, sanitizer-free run recorded them (see mayhem/build.sh, "FAULT-FIDELITY RELAX").
# The rest of ASan+UBSan is on and halting (-fno-sanitize-recover=all).
# origin: https://app.mayhem.security/mayhemheroes/fcc/fcc/14
cmds:
  - cmd: /mayhem/fcc -S /tmp/fcc-input.c
    filepath: /tmp/fcc-input.c
testsuite:
  - https://$MAYHEM_DOMAIN/$MAYHEM_PROJECT/$MAYHEM_TARGET/testsuite.tar
